{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038531-translating-characters-to-mtas-pop-culture","id":1038531,"title":"Translating characters to MtAs (pop culture)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-26T12:50:08-08:00","id":1038531,"title":"Translating characters to MtAs (pop culture)","content":"after reading some comics and novels, i been curious in using expies of popular character's in my games. but im still trying to figure out their stats and spheres. any ideas or suggestions on<br /> Hellboy's Grigori Rasputin<br /> Mr Croup and Mr Vandemar (Neverwhere)<br /> John Constantine (Hellblazer)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:34:13-08:00","id":1040143,"title":"","content":"Don't forget Harry Dresden. Is he a Marauder? Because he never suffers from Paradox and uses some pretty vulgar rotes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:36:05-08:00","id":1040148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038531-translating-characters-to-mtas-pop-culture?p=1040143#post1040143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget Harry Dresden. Is he a Marauder? Because he never suffers from Paradox and uses some pretty vulgar rotes...</div> </div> </div> </div>By that logic every single wizard in Harry Potter is a marauder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:52:52-08:00","id":1040419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038531-translating-characters-to-mtas-pop-culture?p=1040143#post1040143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget Harry Dresden. Is he a Marauder? Because he never suffers from Paradox and uses some pretty vulgar rotes...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerous characters from fiction will never completely fit in M:tA--the metaphysics are too idiosyncratic. You can definitely use them for ideas though. Some examples:<br /> <br /> Gandalf: Demonstrates how limits on paradigm can be cool. He can only use fire in the presence of pre-existing fire, or flammable objects. That kind of limitation creates an interesting style.<br /> <br /> Faust: Classic example of how hubris in dealing wit Umbrood can be tragic.<br /> <br /> Prospero: Classic example about how hubris in dealing with Umbrood can be awesome.<br /> <br /> The 3 witches from Macbeth: Shows the alien way a Mage with Quiet or extreme hubris can behave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:08:05-08:00","id":1040428,"title":"","content":"Harry Dresden is a sorcerer, though a very powerful one, because of the amount of preparation required for his more impressive efforts (though Alchemy and Enchantment seem to take hours rather than days in the Dresden world).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T02:53:11-08:00","id":1040514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038531-translating-characters-to-mtas-pop-culture?p=1040419#post1040419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gandalf: Demonstrates how limits on paradigm can be cool. He can only use fire in the presence of pre-existing fire, or flammable objects. That kind of limitation creates an interesting style.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is rather questionable. Most of the powers we see from Gandalf are him conjuring cheap tricks - ventriloquism against trolls, making explosive pinecones against wargs, making fireworks for hobbits. We know that he's strong enough to beat a Balrog in a duel, but we never see how he actually does that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038531-translating-characters-to-mtas-pop-culture?p=1040419#post1040419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faust: Classic example of how hubris in dealing wit Umbrood can be tragic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Faust and Margarita triumph over Mephistopheles and go to heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T08:18:33-08:00","id":1040675,"title":"","content":"&gt;Harry Dresden is a sorcerer<br /> I think you're going to have to back that up with more than a raw assertion - show some stats or examples.<br /> <br /> I've just been rereading the books and while he mostly uses a well defined set of 'spells' he's a lot more flexible than he seems at first. For example, in White Knight Harry freezes a section of Lake by casting an especially overpowered fire effect in order to help his friends escape from a ghoul attack. That's not the linear, only use it one way, effect that a Sorcerer would have. That's thinking on your feet Sphere magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T21:29:27-08:00","id":1041097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038531-translating-characters-to-mtas-pop-culture?p=1040514#post1040514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is rather questionable. Most of the powers we see from Gandalf are him conjuring cheap tricks - ventriloquism against trolls, making explosive pinecones against wargs, making fireworks for hobbits. We know that he's strong enough to beat a Balrog in a duel, but we never see how he actually does that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm specifically talking about his use of fire here: causing pinecones to burst into flame as you said, and somewhere in LOTR (just the book) redirecting fire from a campfire. Neither is just conjuring fire from nothing. Same with his fireworks: he didn't just make a light show ex nihilo.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038531-translating-characters-to-mtas-pop-culture?p=1040514#post1040514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both Faust and Margarita triumph over Mephistopheles and go to heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>In some versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}